  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets are finite?\n\n- $P(N)$\n- $P({Z,\\pi })$\n- $P({x\\in Z\u2223\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=0})$",
  "worked_solution": "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is infinite since the underlying set $N$ is infinite.\n\n- Set II is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,\\pi })={\u2205,\\,{Z},\\,{\\pi },\\,{Z,\\pi }}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{x\\in Z\u2223\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=0}={0},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({x\\in Z\u2223\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=0})=P({0})={\u2205,\\,{0}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
